        },
        {
          "name": "Task Function",
          "type": "TaskFunctionType&&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<TaskFunctionType> void",
      "docs": "Push a new task.\n@param DebugName    Helps to identify the task in debugger and profiler.\n@param TaskFunction A callable with a slot parameter, usually a lambda but can be also a functor object\nor a pointer to a function. The slot parameter is an index in [0..max_concurrency) range,\nunique at any moment of time, that can be used in user code to index a fixed-size buffer.\nSee `TaskConcurrencyLimiterStressTest()` for an example."
    },
    {
      "id": "wait",
      "name": "Wait",
      "category": "TaskConcurrencyLimiter",
      "signature": "Wait(Target, Timeout)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FTaskConcurrencyLimiter*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Timeout",
          "type": "FTimespan"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Bool",
      "docs": "Waits for task's completion with timeout.\n@param  Timeout Maximum amount of time to wait for tasks to finish before returning.\n@return true if all tasks are completed, false otherwise.\n@note   A wait is satisfied once the internal task counter reaches 0 and is never reset\nafterward when more tasks are added. A new FTaskConcurrencyLimiter can be used\nfor such a use case."
    },
